abstract: >-
  The ITEA Framework provides ten complementary indicators covering 1,016 SOC 6-digit
  occupations from O*NET 30.2, designed to measure occupational exposure to algorithmic
  expropriation in the Agentic AI regime. Version 3.0 introduces three major methodological
  revisions motivated by a documented case study of three research papers (the trilogy
  8A/8B/8C): z-score ITEA aggregation, triple-residualised IRA, and a dual-variant OAEI
  architecture. External convergent validation against the AIOE benchmark of Felten,
  Raj and Seamans (2021): r(OAEI v3.0+, AIOE) = 0.797 over 738 common SOC 6-digit
  occupations.
